# Allowlist for `mypy.stubtest`, read by scripts/run-all-checks.sh and CI.
#
# The supported imports are "from host_new_horizons import ..." and
# "from host_new_horizons.oops import ...", so the stubs of those two packages describe
# the whole public API. host_new_horizons.oops imports the module below, which is
# implementation detail and deliberately carries no stub; stubtest reports it as "failed
# to find stubs", which this file accepts. Nothing else is accepted: a public name missing from the two
# stubs still fails the check.
host_new_horizons\.oops\.lorri
